 ✅✅ TCP/IP fundamentals
************************************************************

🔹  TCP/IP is a protocal that helps computers to communicate over a network
🔹  TCP/IP is not a single protocal . It is collection of different protocals like
   >> UDP, HTTP, HTTPS, TCP, FTP, SSH, ICMP, ARP, DNS
🔹🔹 1. TCP/IP layer
+--------------------+
| Application Layer  |
| HTTP HTTPS DNS SSH |
+--------------------+
| Transport Layer    |
| TCP UDP            |
+--------------------+
| Internet Layer     |
| IP ICMP            |
+--------------------+
| Network Layer      |
| Ethernet ARP       |
+--------------------+
🔹🔹 2. TCP Three-Way Handshake
Step 1: SYN   Client starts connection
Step 2: SYN ACK Server replies
Step 3: ACK Client sends
Client                     Server

SYN ----------->
       <-------- SYN ACK

ACK ----------->
🔹🔹 Use of Sequence numbers in TCP communication
Detect loss
Detect duplicates
Maintain order
Retransmit packets

🔹🔹 3. Flow control
🔹 Sender may be much faster than receiver, sender = 1GB , receiver 100MB
🔹 To avoid this problem receiver advertise receiver windows ex: 800 bytes, send only 800 bytes and wait for ACK
    >> Window = 8000 bytes
🔹 Flow control protects receiver by avoiding congestion control

🔹🔹 4. UDP Vs TCP
  >> TCP
      Connection Oriented
      Reliable
      Ordered
      Retransmission
      Error Recovery
  >> Example protocals
     HTTPS, SSH, SMTP , SFTP
  >> UDP
      No Connection
      No ACK
      No Retransmission
      Faster
      Lower Overhead
🔹🔹 5. Why Ports Exist?
    >> One machine runs many applications.
    22    SSH
    80    HTTP
    443   HTTPS
    53    DNS
    25    SMTP
🔹🔹 6. Socket
   >> Socket is a end point of comminucation and is a combination of IP-address and port
